# Logs and scratch
*.log
docker-build.log

# Source corpus. Not version controlled: 49 vendored HTML pages made up 85% of
# the repository and rendered it "84.8% HTML" on GitHub, which describes the
# scraped documentation rather than the project. It is fully reproducible -
# rebuild with `python tools/fetch_corpus.py`.
DATA/

# Superseded architecture docs. The README is the single source of truth; these
# still described Portkey, withdrawn Llama models and the Streamlit UI, none of
# which the system uses. Recoverable from git history if ever needed.
DOCS/

# Editor and agent tooling, machine-specific (absolute .venv paths).
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and worth stating why:
#
#   evals/dataset/            the golden dataset is ground truth; a change to it
#                             must show up in review like any other change.
#   evals/runs/               evaluation artifacts. Published numbers that
#                             nobody can re-open are not evidence, which is why
#                             the previous suite's results existed only in
#                             Streamlit session state.
#   evals/baseline*.json      the thresholds CI gates on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
